**What Nevada law says (from PropInspect's guide):**
- **Deadline:** The landlord has 30 days after your lease ends and you move out to return the deposit or send an itemized written list of deductions.
- **Penalty:** If they don't return it on time, you can recover the whole deposit, plus up to the same amount again in court-ordered damages (up to 2x in total).
- **Legal basis:** Nevada Revised Statutes § 118A.242 ([official text](https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-118A.html#NRS118ASec242)).

